WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.750
To demonstrate their military power to JIOR, their father country,

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.460
and to unveil the secrets of the Valvraves,

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:11.030
Tokishima Haruto and his comrades descended to Earth.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.700
But the Dorssian army intercepted them,

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.200
and they ended up crashing in Dorssian territory.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.630
There, Haruto found his father, who turned out to be the head of the Valvrave project.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.920
Marie, who turned out to have been a test pilot, died.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.340
They then discovered The Phantom was collecting runes from humans.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.500
And the light L-Elf was seeking, Lieselotte,

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.110
turned out to be an alien creature, a Magius.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:54.140
She told Haruto about the Council of the Hundred and One.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:59.120
a secret society of humans and Magius
manipulating the world from behind the scenes.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.040
As Haruto and his friends sought to discover the mystery of the Valvraves,

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.290
they began to uncover a much greater mystery surrounding the whole world.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.190
But as it stands, they must return home...

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:24.570
They found out that the Phantom is headed for Module 77.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:43.660
Found it.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.370
Speed 16. It's headed for the debris cloud.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.260
Gonna shoot it down before it reaches Module 77!

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.040
Firing angle adjusted.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.780
Calibrating launch timing.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.020
Five seconds. Three. Two. One.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.270
Eat shit!

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.610
It didn't hit!

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.770
Who was it?! Someone said if the two of them fired at once, at least one of them would hit!

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.780
Yeah, I did... Crap.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.120
It's not working!

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.030
That's insane! There's no way he can catch up!

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.250
You'll overheat if you keep going at that speed!

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.010
There's no other choice!

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.150
Reach it!

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:08.510
You did it!

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:11.080
That was awesome, Haruto!

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.460
We got lucky. It won't work the next time.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:20.410
But this is the best we can do for now.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:26.200
We've lost his help, after all.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.710
Haruto!

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:25.050
Haruto! I'm so glad!

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.140
Shoko. I'm glad to see you in one piece.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.510
There's so much I wanna tell you!

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.230
Wanna hear?

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.220
Welcome back, Kibukawa!

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:40.360
It's great to be back.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.480
Any problems while I was gone?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.750
We managed!

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.670
The students worked really hard.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.180
Who are they?

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:53.740
Ah, them? JIORian scientists.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.750
They were captured by the Dorssians, so we rescued them.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.120
Scientists?

00:05:58.450 --> 00:05:59.250
Iori!

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.590
Iori! Iori!

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:05.840
Dad?

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.280
Am I dreaming?

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.450
Dad!

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:11.030
I'm sorry, Iori.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.950
It wasn't supposed to turn out like this.

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.230
I'm so sorry!

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.040
Why are you apologizing?

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.970
I don't get it.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.650
I'm so relieved. It's a miracle.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.660
Jesus.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.700
That almost brought a tear to my eye.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.730
Yamada!

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:33.010
Are you Yamada Raizou? The Valvrave pilot!

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.700
That's Thunder for you!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:35.540
Who are you?

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:39.290
Barlet, from Golden News. You don't know me?

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.990
Not a clue. How should I know you?

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:44.300
He's a famous journalist!

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.250
I asked him to do this!

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:50.300
There's a weekly documentary about us airing in ARUS.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:53.740
We've got a lot of new supporters!

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:56.560
They send us lots of donations and supplies.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.940
We're not making anything mopey.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:04.250
It's only thanks to your hard work that you've gotten more support.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:14.570
Assuming that I hadn't engaged in the fight with Q-Vier and fled instead,

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:17.950
they would've attacked us from behind. I would've been drained.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.740
The conclusion is—

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.330
No.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:25.210
Was it even earlier?

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:30.540
The timing to rescuing her. The method of getting out of the tower.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:33.270
Buying time until Tokishima Haruto arrived.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.650
No...

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.290
There was no way I could've saved her.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.650
The conclusion is...

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:53.460
darkness.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:59.160
Resistance activity is flaring up all around Dorssia.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:04.540
The Valvraves seem to have shaken the people's trust in the army.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:09.550
It appears as if the calm masses have suddenly risen up.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:16.430
Will Princess Lieselotte's death make her a martyr for the royalists?

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:17.880
I don't know.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:22.560
In the meantime, what should we do about the captured Valvrave pilot?

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:25.980
Rukino Saki...?

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:51.840
I still can't believe Marie's left us forever.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.210
Did you give up on the way?

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:56.060
Honestly, a bunch of times.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.970
But my friends were always there by my side.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:01.210
Your escape from Dorssiana was quite a feat.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.050
Using a shuttle from a museum is pretty unconventional.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:06.860
Well, it was left pretty unscathed in storage. But even more so, it was a race against time.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:09.480
My apt timing was key to success.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:15.490
As the team returns to Earth, they bring with them the burden of grief.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:22.910
But with grief comes renewed confidence in themselves.

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:19.610
We're on the telly, man!

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:22.560
I heard we have the highest rating out of all the news programs.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.900
The Beast Up folk praised us too.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.560
Seems they've doubled their sales thanks to us.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.310
Insurance companies have made offers, too—

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.510
Who gives a damn about TV?

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.890
Didn't you see the Phantom?

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:37.670
They're regularly feeding on humans!

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:41.510
Just like I do.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:43.840
Calm down, Haruto.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:46.270
Rukino's still on Earth, too.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:51.660
The whole mess with the Magius and the Council of the Hundred and One is left to us as well.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:53.580
And where are they?

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:57.400
We had a look when Akira hacked the Phantom.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:01.450
Judging from the ship's number, there's over a hundred Phantoms out there.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.100
But we have no other clues.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:10.200
We can't even locate the enemy, so how do you intend to fight them?

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:12.170
Do you have a plan?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.160
A plan...

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.810
Just accept reality.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.610
We must do what we can for now.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.950
Do you dislike fame?

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:35.070
You're definitely famous. But fame is a fleeting thing.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:40.370
In a year, you might become just another person on the street.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.950
What's your point?

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:43.950
Do you think you can win?

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:49.770
Unlike the viewers, Dorssia won't sympathize with you.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:54.340
You don't have the overwhelming military
advantage to retake the JIORian fatherland.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:57.340
Mr. Barnet, don't put it that way...

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.950
Did you ever think that you're Don Quixote?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.550
That Dorssia is a gargantuan windmill?

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:08.560
I don't know.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.570
You're so mean.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:23.520
I've interviewed a number of successful revolutionaries before.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:27.430
They shared one aspect — they were all naive.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.720
These were H-Neun's.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:43.970
Who wants the belongings of a traitor?

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.970
They were the same colors as our hair?

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:51.850
If he was this devoted, why would he betray us?

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:53.850
Hey, that—

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:57.110
It's mine.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:11:59.520
Whatever.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:06.090
<i>Did you really betray us?</i>

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:12.750
Thanks for your help. Now we can get to repairing Unit 3.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.410
At least let us atone for what we did.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:16.250
Thanks.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:21.260
I'm still impressed these units were completed.

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:28.820
Yeah... I wish we had a choice besides using this technology.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.190
L-Elf!

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.120
I know you're there.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.980
I'm by myself.

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:43.030
I'm coming in.

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:49.950
I want you to help us. You heard about the Council of—

00:12:58.270 --> 00:12:59.340
What the...

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:05.470
I couldn't save her in any of my simulations.

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:11.880
Lieselotte!

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:23.220
Um, Lieselotte...

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:29.380
Get out. There's nothing you can do.

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:39.670
L-Elf... I'll come again.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:49.670
There's nothing more to do.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.520
L-Elf might need some time.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.150
Yeah...

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:00.550
But Haruto, don't worry about it.

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:01.320
Still...

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:03.420
I know it's tough.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:08.680
The Magius. Rescuing Rukino. The Phantoms.

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:10.940
There are just too many problems.

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:14.140
There's your father, too.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:20.490
But there's nothing we can sort out right away.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.010
Right?

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:29.260
You should just go on a date with Shoko or something.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:30.840
You need to take your mind off things.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.930
How could I — with everything that's going on?!

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:36.060
That's exactly why you need to.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:40.440
Nobody knows when we'll bite the dust.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:45.110
In the face of death, people can do anything.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.070
Just don't leave any regrets.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:50.760
Right.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:56.280
Ah, here you are! I've been looking everywhere for you!

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:57.330
Shoko?

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.180
Well, I'll catch you guys later.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:00.710
But—

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:02.210
Where are you going?

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.710
I'm about to pass out. Night!

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:06.250
Good night!

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.450
Good night...

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.130
He must be tired.

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:13.790
You were looking for me?

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:15.470
Oh, right! I have big news!

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.980
They voted to condemn Dorssia for the attack!

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:23.230
We've been pushing for this forever!

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:27.650
When Shoko brought it up, we thought it was never gonna happen.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:30.780
But then, we were in the center of it!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.660
ARUS sided with us, too.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.670
And not only ARUS! 84 other countries, too!

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:38.830
Not even Dorssia can ignore that.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:42.110
The presidential elections in ARUS are coming up, as well.

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:45.980
Elections in a democracy are just a popularity contest.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:51.230
If they ignore the condemning vote, then sanctions will follow.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:54.880
Dorssia will have no chance but to negotiate.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:55.970
That's why you called the news station?

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.240
At first I was turned down by everyone I went to.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:02.260
Even Mr. Barnet did — three times.

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:04.540
But we kept looking people up and called them.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.730
Eventually, some people agreed to help!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:10.240
I see. You were all fighting, too.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:11.900
It's all thanks to you!

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:13.320
Me?

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.260
Yeah. Back in that cave...

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:24.170
It's fine, Shoko. I'm here with you.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.840
I'll stay here with you, okay?

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:34.090
And you did come back. I believed in you!

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:10.140
But this success won't change anything immediately.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:13.900
We've gotta work hard on it, one step at a time.

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:15.260
Together.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:21.770
So... L-Elf... I'll be waiting for you, too.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.960
I'm leaving your food here.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:36.780
The international summit soon to be opened at Module 77 will be held in a complicated political atmosphere,

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:36.780
H-Neun... Who could kill you?

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:40.950
but we can say for certain that it will go down in history.

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:42.990
After all, the battle of children—

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:44.170
What?!

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.150
We should go.

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:02.740
But...

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:06.200
Let's leave this to others.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:07.940
What do you mean?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.060
Someone gave me a tip.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.190
What?!

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.080
If it's true, this is gonna get ugly.

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:14.480
But it's insane!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.390
Where's Eileen?

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.240
I haven't seen her since this morning.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:26.250
We would like to thank everyone for joining us in our country today.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:30.670
I'm sorry, but this gymnasium is the only place we can offer for this international conference.

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.880
This is the current state of JIOR.

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:35.920
We are aware.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.380
Let's begin the conference.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.390
Thank you for your understanding.

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:44.090
Those children went too far.

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:47.060
We didn't expect them to seize a Phantom.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:52.400
It's likely that Lieselotte told them about us.

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:57.830
Our rule is to interfere with the world as little as possible,

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:02.780
but we need them to leave the stage.

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:15.450
All right! All right!

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.840
So this is the Ardor Grip?

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.720
It really makes the operating time 2.4 times longer?

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:41.360
If Professor Kitagawa didn't tell us about it, it'd still be gathering dust in the storage room.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.940
Where did Professor Kitagawa go, anyway?

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:46.620
The other people are gone, too.

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:49.750
Aren't they in the meeting room?

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.760
That's what I was told,

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.630
but no one was there.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:55.420
No one?

00:19:56.480 --> 00:20:00.570
It's unfortunate that Dorssia couldn't send their representatives—

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:01.530
No.

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:08.720
Please allow me to participate.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.360
What's going on?

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:12.060
This wasn't planned!

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:15.690
Please forgive this faux pas,

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:20.200
as there is something I want to show the world.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:25.200
Rukino!

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:28.620
I believe you all know her name.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:33.620
She is a student from Module 77 and a Valvrave pilot.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:33.230
Rukino?

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.210
They caught her?

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.210
She is Rukino Saki.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:43.720
It is a well-known fact that she and her comrades have been fighting us, Dorssia.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:47.660
But from the first moment, I had my doubts.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:54.140
How could ordinary students stand their ground and even win against us?

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:02.490
No way!

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:04.860
Watch and see!

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.240
This is their secret!

00:21:50.680 --> 00:21:52.320
Her wound is gone!

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:53.580
What's going on?!

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.710
What just happened?

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:57.740
She's alive?

00:21:57.740 --> 00:21:58.920
She should be dead!

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:58.920
She's alive!

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:00.090
She revived?!

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:01.100
She's fine?

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:02.050
And her wound?

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.590
I don't get it, either!

00:22:03.930 --> 00:22:04.880
She's alive?

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:07.090
But he stabbed her through the heart!

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:08.990
Is this some trick?

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:12.410
No, it looked real...

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:14.200
This can't be!

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:17.950
Is this some special effect?

00:22:17.950 --> 00:22:19.610
It's insane!

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:26.740
Prime Minister Sashinami, what is the meaning of this?!

00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:31.950
I hope you can see now.

